mailove (2.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Forward as attachment: forwards the message being read as a message/rfc822
    attachment — the original bytes untouched, every image, attachment and
    signature intact and nothing re-rendered. In the message context menu, for
    a single message.
  * Copy as Markdown: select part of an HTML message and copy it as Markdown
    rather than as flattened plain text.
  * HTML to plain text rewritten: layout tables, lists and block structure now
    survive the conversion instead of collapsing, and runs of blank lines are
    capped. Used everywhere text is rendered — the text view, plain-text
    quoting, and the body the spam rules read.
  * Reply and forward quotes stream into the composer a batch per event-loop
    tick, so the composer opens instantly on a newsletter-sized message and
    stays responsive while the quote fills in. Send and Save as draft flush
    what is still pending first.
  * Remote content in a quote is neutralized on a parsed document rather than
    with regexes over markup: remote images and backgrounds go, only data:,
    file: and cid: references survive. Where remote content was allowed, the
    images are prefetched and embedded as cid: parts at send time, per image,
    without the send ever waiting on the network.
  * The composer's modified check compares the document revision instead of
    serializing the whole body to HTML, which blocked the GUI for the better
    part of a second on a large message.
  * Spam scoring decodes RFC 2047 headers before judging them. Encoded-word
    subjects were invisible to the homoglyph and confusable rules — precisely
    the mail those rules exist for.
  * List mail is recognised where the link rules read it, and a rule that
    fired only on ordinary mail was dropped rather than weakened.

