mailove (2.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Spam detection rewritten around the message rather than the X-Spam headers:
    brand impersonation in the sender name, sender-name and URL homograph and
    zero-width tricks, credential-trick and brand-lookalike links, password
    forms in the body, web pages and password-protected archives sent as
    attachments, and the business-email-compromise shape of a corporate sender
    with a freemail Reply-To.
  * Attachment and link rules now actually run. They existed but the client
    only ever scored headers, so nothing that needed a body could fire; a
    message is scored again once its body is in hand.
  * ARC is read, so mailing lists are no longer marked. A list breaks SPF and
    DKIM by design and ARC carries the verdict from before it did.
  * Three rules that fired on ordinary mail are gone or weakened, measured
    against a real mailbox: Message-ID and Return-Path naming a different
    domain than From (61% and 6% of ordinary mail — every mailing platform
    does both, and SPF already authorises it) and Reply-To mismatches.
  * A brand cannot impersonate itself: links to a sender's own asset and
    shortener domains are no longer read as lookalikes.
  * The red ! now means spam and only spam. Hovering lists every rule that
    fired with its weight and the total the verdict was made from.
  * Everything in the junk folder is marked, including mail filed there before
    any of this existed.
  * Scoring runs in the inbox and the junk folder only — never Sent, Drafts or
    Trash, and never in imported archives, whose mail lacks the headers the
    rules assume and would be marked for being old.
  * Taking a message out of the junk folder allowlists the sender, whether by
    the Not-spam action or by moving it; Not spam also puts it back in the
    inbox instead of leaving it buried.
  * Sent and Drafts show To instead of From, sort by it, and search it.
  * A one-time cache migration fills that column in from mail already on disk,
    with a progress dialog. Nothing is re-downloaded.
  * The message list no longer waits for an unrelated event to notice that the
    open folder changed.
  * A clipboard image that cannot be pasted into a message says why instead of
    doing nothing.

