mailove (2.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ctrl+V puts a picture from the clipboard into the message where the
    cursor is, instead of only being able to attach one as a file. It travels
    with the message as an inline part, survives saving and reopening a draft,
    and is sent as an attachment on plain-text accounts, which have no body
    that can reference it.
  * New Layout setting: the message preview can sit below the message list as
    before, or beside it. Each layout remembers its own divider position, and
    the folder pane width is now remembered too.
  * In the beside layout the list shows each message on two lines, sender and
    date above subject, separated by a hairline rule; sorting moves to a
    button next to the search field and stays in step with the column
    headers of the other layout.
  * Search works offline and in imported archives instead of refusing with
    "Not connected" — the local index is the search when no server can be
    reached.
  * A search that found nothing no longer leaves a filter behind that hid the
    results of the next one, and clearing a search offline restores the
    folder instead of leaving the hits on screen.
  * Typing in the search field no longer resets the message list on every
    keystroke.
  * Settings help texts rewritten throughout: shorter, and all at one size.
    The JMAP note no longer claims that marking read, moving, deleting and
    sending are unimplemented — they are.
  * Simplified application icon.

