mailove (2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * JMAP support (RFC 8620/8621). An account now chooses its protocol: IMAP
    as before, or JMAP, which discovers its own endpoints from the address
    and authenticates with an API token or a password. Both kinds of account
    can be configured at once.
  * Mail protocols sit behind one interface, so which mailbox is the trash,
    when to backfill and what a header means are answered the same way
    whichever protocol replied. Push arrives as IMAP IDLE or JMAP
    EventSource and is handled identically.
  * Fixed: migrating an account from a pre-1.0 install silently reset its
    IMAP port to 993, its security to SSL/TLS and lost its SMTP settings.
    The values were read from the wrong settings scope.
  * Fixed: after the wallet lookup finished, a connection requested while it
    was still in flight was never resumed, so the client could sit offline
    with a perfectly good account configured.
  * Fixed: a DKIM or OpenPGP verdict on a message rebuilt from the cache
    could be attributed to whichever message was on screen when a delayed
    retry landed, reporting cache staleness as tampering.
  * Quieter status bar: breadcrumbs that only repeated what the window
    already showed (an empty folder, a link opening in the browser) are gone
    from the status line and kept in the debug log.
  * Internals: the mail controller is split into an account store, a sync
    engine, a cache-maintenance scheduler, a message presenter and a
    signature verifier, each testable on its own. The test suite grew to
    twelve binaries covering the cache, account storage and the attachment
    split/restore pair.

