mailove (1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Unread counts in the folder pane: a pill on every folder, blue on the
    inbox, and an outline on a collapsed folder standing in for the unread
    sitting in subfolders folded away beneath it.
  * Other accounts are checked for new mail on the refresh schedule — connect,
    STATUS, disconnect — so their unread counts move without switching to them.
  * Spam retention (Settings, General): mail sent longer ago than the chosen
    number of days is removed from the spam folder automatically, going by the
    date the message carries. "Skip trash for spam" (on by default) deletes it
    outright rather than filing it in the trash to be cleared out twice.
  * Folders can be dragged onto another folder to reparent them, or onto the
    account name to move them to the top level. Imported archives included.
  * Rename folder in the folder context menu. Where the protocol forbids it —
    INBOX, and the special-use mailboxes a server recreates — the menu says so
    in place of the command.
  * Message context menu, starting with Mark unread. A message marked unread
    while open stays open and stays unread; it is marked read again the next
    time it is opened.
  * A "No label" key that clears any colour label, alongside the five.
  * Junk is called spam throughout the interface, except where a folder is
    named otherwise by the server.
  * Fixes: an account switch no longer carries the previous account's folder
    delimiter, which could rewrite an imported archive's folder paths; folder
    trees keep parents directly above their children; folders in the sidebar
    could not be dragged at all.

